Up here, then. Two things that are not on any map.

§**Saves.**§ A real world writes itself down as you play and waits in there for
you. Ours did not -- nothing you just did was kept, which is rather the point
of a practice island.
---
@Signals Officer
:: point=menu.2
§**Multiplayer.**§ One machine hosts and everyone else joins it. A turn
resolves when every player has said they are ready, so a game moves at the
speed of whoever is slowest.

Play with people who answer their messages.
